<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stono Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1739</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stono Rebellion was a revolt of enslaved Africans that began on 9 September 1739 near the Stono River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>. Led by a man named Jemmy, many of the rebels came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a>; they killed about 20 colonists and marched towards Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, which offered freedom, before militia defeated them. It was the largest slave revolt in the British mainland colonies, and the Negro Act of 1740 imposed harsher controls.</p></div>
